  "body": "The path data of a canvas is currently very inaccessible other than modifying its value.  You aren't able to retrieve the path if you wanted to use it on another canvas.\r\n\r\n```webidl\r\nvoid setPath(Path2D path);\r\n[NewObject] Path2D getPath();\r\n```\r\n\r\nUsing `fill(Path2D)`/`stroke(Path2D)` allows you to draw the path, but it doesn't let you continue drawing from the final point of that path since it is just drawn and not applied.  As an example, if my path was an `arc`/`ellipse`, I wouldn't be able to continue drawing from the final point in the `arc`/`ellipse` path without modifying the path.  Using `setPath`, I would instead be able to apply the path to the canvas and then modify the canvas' path without affecting the parameter path.",
